# FIXTURE — NOT LIVE CODE, never sourced or executed. Positive control for #197 instance 5.
#
# The pre-fix pod-side single-quoted PROMPT of agents/reviewer-session.sh (commit 1698b42 parent,
# 2026-08-18 ~17:37Z → fixed 18:27Z). The PROMPT='…' assignment sits INSIDE the body of the
# EXPANDING `PREP=$(cat <<PREP` heredoc — the whole body is shipped to the review pod and executed,
# so the apostrophe in "sandbox's" terminates the single-quoted string and everything after it
# parses as shell. Every reviewer pod since #547 merged died on "bash: -c: line 144: syntax error
# near unexpected token '('" and then reported Succeeded (the uploader trap masks the exit).
# EXPECT: SQ-PROSE@14
#
PREP=$(cat <<PREP
set -e
gh repo clone ${REPO_SLUG} /work/repo
PROMPT='Review pull request #${PR}.

  TOOL GAPS (homelab#536) — name one only where the absence actually changed your verdict, and
  never this sandbox's deliberate lack of devbox/network (that is the design above, not a gap).
  The verdict question is NOT "is this perfect?" — it is "is master better off WITH this PR?"'
PREP
)
